From 224e4aca31cc1195dc4ce57bc51198379b82b1fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Tomasz=20Kami=C5=84ski?= <tkaminsk@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:37:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: Fix inplace_vector capacity checks for oversized
 ranges.

The inplace_vector's _S_distance check, was unconditionally casting
range size into the size_type. For oversized ranges, whose difference_type
and is larger size_t, this trims the value, and may lead to false acceptance
of range of size that is greater than capacity.

This patch, addresses the above, by replacing above with S_distance_if_fits
function, that also checks capacity. The checks are performed by _S_check_size
and _S_check_distance functions. The former is templated on integer type,
and performs the cast only after verifying that range size fits in the
capacity (and thus in size_type).

For _S_check_distance, stops iterating the range after capacity() - size()
elements, instead of calling std::distance. The change is also applied
to the range overloads, via newly defined _S_distance_if_fits overload.

Finally, the runtime if on _S_distance (false_type was returned in case
of input iterators), is replaced with the if constexpr. Previously both
branches were emitted for forward (or stronger iterator), as else branch
was triggered for ranges of size zero. The constraints are extracted to
new __any_sizeable_iterator concept (mirroring __any_input_iterator).

libstdc++-v3/ChangeLog:

	* include/bits/stl_iterator_base_types.h (__any_sizeable_iterator):
	Define.
	* include/std/inplace_vector (inplace_vector::_S_reserve):
	Replace with...
	(inplace_vector::_S_check_size, inplace_vector::_S_check_distance):
	Define.
	(inplace_vector::_S_distance): Replace with..
	(inplace_vector::_S_distance_if_fits): Rework _S_distance with
	integrated bounds checking, and overloaded for rangs.
	(inplace_vector::reserve, inplace_vector::resize): Replace
	_S_reserve with _S_check_size.
	(inplace_vector::inplace_vector, inplace_vector::assign): Replace
	runtime check with if constexpr and use _S_distance_if_fits.
	(inplace_vector::insert): Likewise, and skip rotate for insertion
	at the end.
	(inplace_vector::append_range): Use _S_distance_if_fits to compute
	size.
	* testsuite/23_containers/inplace_vector/modifiers/capacity_check.cc:
	New test.

Reviewed-by: Jonathan Wakely <jwakely@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 404fb73f95f44a2930066c7948c983d3f58572da)
